    "@type" : "Question",
    "name" : "Transfer Pricing compliance and documentation&nbsp;",
    "acceptedAnswer" : {
      "@type" : "Answer",
      "text" : "<p><b>We provide comprehensive TP compliance and documentation services to help clients meet regulatory requirements while aligning with global best practices.</b></p>\r\n<p>Our services include the preparation of local files, master files, and country-by-country reports in accordance with Indian regulations and OECD Transfer Pricing guidelines. We assist in developing robust documentation that supports the arm’s length nature of intercompany transactions, minimizing audit risks and facilitating transparency. Our team works closely with clients to understand their business models and deliver tailored documentation. With deep technical knowledge and industry insights, our specialists help clients stay compliant, reduce penalty exposure, and navigate evolving regulatory landscapes.</p>"
    }
  }, {
    "@type" : "Question",
    "name" : "Transfer Pricing planning and operating model effectiveness",
    "acceptedAnswer" : {
      "@type" : "Answer",
      "text" : "<p><b>We support clients in designing and implementing effective TP policies that are aligned with their commercial objectives and global value chains.</b></p>\r\n<p>We translate business strategies into compliant and efficient TP frameworks with input from tax, customs, and accounting professionals.&nbsp;We provide functional and risk analyses, benchmarking, pricing model design, and alignment of intercompany agreements. We facilitate seamless policy integration into daily operations, enabling multi-jurisdictional consistency. We help businesses future-proof their TP strategies sustainably in a complex regulatory environment through value contribution analysis.</p>"
    }
  }, {
    "@type" : "Question",
    "name" : "Base Erosion and Profit Shifting 2.0: Pillar II",
    "acceptedAnswer" : {
      "@type" : "Answer",
      "text" : "<p><b>As jurisdictions around the world begin implementing global minimum tax rules under the OECD’s Pillar Two framework, multinational enterprises (MNEs) should proactively prepare for significant changes.</b></p>\r\n<p>Organizations are still in the early stages of transition to Pillar Two and face the challenge of calculating new tax liabilities, assessing financial statement impacts, and meeting complex global reporting obligations. We support clients through this transformation by providing impact assessments, gap analyses, and implementation support, helping them navigate the evolving global tax landscape with confidence.</p>"
    }
  }, {
    "@type" : "Question",
    "name" : "Transfer Pricing controversy management and dispute resolution",
    "acceptedAnswer" : {
      "@type" : "Answer",
      "text" : "<p><b>In an era of heightened transparency and information sharing among tax authorities, we offer comprehensive controversy management services to help clients navigate complex TP disputes with confidence and strategic clarity.</b></p>\r\n<p>We support clients through the full controversy lifecycle—from audit readiness and representation before tax and appellate authorities to resolution through APAs and MAPs. Our team blends technical knowledge with practical dispute experience, delivering tailored strategies that mitigate risk and drive sustainable outcomes in a highly regulated global tax environment.</p>"
    }
  }, {
    "@type" : "Question",
    "name" : "Digital solution offerings",
    "acceptedAnswer" : {
      "@type" : "Answer",
      "text" : "<p><b>We integrate advanced technology into our TP services to drive accuracy, efficiency, and compliance.</b></p>\r\n<p>Our digital solutions help automate complex processes, enhance data management, and provide real-time insights—empowering businesses to meet regulatory compliance requirements, manage risks, and align TP operations with evolving global tax standards. Our key tools include:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><b>RPT Automation Solution: </b>Our proprietary platform automates the tracking, reconciliation, and compliance of related party transactions across Companies Act, SEBI LODR guidelines, and the Income-tax Act, 1961. It centralizes data, enhances governance, and streamlines reporting. By reducing manual effort and facilitating audit-ready documentation, RPT Automation Solution helps businesses mitigate compliance risks and efficiently meet disclosure requirements.<br>\r\n&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><b>DigiRev™:</b> A proprietary digital solution designed to collate evidence for intra-group services and royalty transactions by scanning emails and extracting relevant information using customized keyword algorithms. DigiRev™ enhances documentation quality, reduces manual effort, and improves data security. <a href=\"https://www.ey.com/en_in/services/tax/digital-strategy/digirev\">https://www.ey.com/en_in/services/tax/digital-strategy/digirev</a><br>\r\n&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><b>TP Web™: </b>Our documentation platform helps meet BEPS Action 13 requirements through efficient, group-wide preparation of master and local files. It accommodates varying documentation structures and integrates with ERP systems for centralized, automated data collection. Customizable features—such as user-specific access and tailored reporting—enable scalable, secure monitoring and assessment, enhancing consistency, transparency, and compliance.<br>\r\n&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><b>TP Engine: </b>Our ready-to-deploy Operational Transfer Pricing platform is built on SAP and powered by a dedicated tax and TP data model. It manages intercompany transactions end-to-end—covering service allocations, royalties, profit splits, cost sharing, and supply chain analytics. With robust reporting and smart data ingestion, it enables adjustments, journal entries, and price list generation, improving transparency, automation, and compliance across jurisdictions.<br>\r\n&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><b>CbCR Web™:</b> Our dedicated Country-by-Country Reporting (CbCR) tool is developed to support MNEs in meeting CbCR compliance requirements. It enables efficient centralized and automated data collection, validation, and management of CbCr reporting data by seamlessly integrating with commonly used ERP systems. Designed for scalability and accuracy, CbCR Web™ streamlines XML report preparation, automates data aggregation, and aligns with local filing standards.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>"
    }
  } ]
}

